{"type":"finding","severity":"minor","fileName":"BasisRustServer/crates/basis-server-core/src/lib.rs","title":"Count relayed scene sends in `statistics.outboundpackets`.","comment":"**Count relayed scene sends in `statistics.outbound_packets`.**

The previous path called `send_to_recipients_or_broadcast`, which used `ServerState::broadcast`. `broadcast` increments `statistics.outbound_packets` for each successful `transport.send`. The new path returns from `relay.enqueue(...)`, and `send_target` in `scene_relay.rs` never touches `Statistics`. If `BASIS_SCENE_BATCH_MS` is 1 or 2, `AppOut` / `App messages: outbound=` no longer counts unreliable SCENE broadcasts. That traffic is usually the largest scene fan-out. As a result, operators who compare runs with batching on and off see a false drop in outbound traffic.

To fix this, pass a clone of `state.statistics` into `SceneRelay::start` (`Statistics` is `Clone` and holds `Arc` counters). In `send_target`, add `count` on a successful send so the logical-message semantics match `broadcast`.

